      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rollins%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Situated just north of the Flathead Indian Reservation, Rollins sits on Flathead Lake’s west shore at 2,983 feet elevation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rollins%2C_Montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The early 1900s homestead boom turned the former Bay View into a thriving timber town that also grew apple and cherry orchards.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mtmemory.org/nodes/view/128492"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Two miles northeast of Rollins lies Medicine Rock, a Kootenai sacred site that once marked a battlefield where the tribe defeated the Blackfeet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/rollins_montana"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "From its 2,936‑foot perch, Rollins offers sweeping views of the Rocky Mountains and easy access to Flathead Lake’s 185‑mile shoreline.",
